Coalesce repeated Solaris event-port wakeups.

Unlike eventfd and pipe-backed wakers, port_send(3C) queues every user event.
Tokio can therefore build an unbounded queue of identical reactor wakeups. A
busy runtime then repeatedly receives full event batches and can starve normal
I/O processing.

Track pending user-event tokens in the selector state. Repeated wakes for an
already pending token are covered by the queued event, and processing the event
clears the token before returning it to the caller. The mutex orders concurrent
wakes with event consumption so a wake is either coalesced into the event being
delivered or queues a new event.

Add a regression that verifies repeated wake calls produce one event and leave
no second event queued.

